'''Razón y Justicia''' ({{Literal translation|Reason and Justice}}; '''RJ''') is a [[W:Platformism|platform]] in Balisca founded on 8 January 2024. It has been described as a [[W:Left-wing politics|left-wing]] to [[W:Far-left politics|far-left]] party with [[W:Left-wing populism|populist]] and [[W:Left-wing nationalism|nationalist]] tendencies. The RJ is skeptical of {{W|free migration}}, criticizes the [[Kuluba Accords]], and holds [[w:Anti-imperialism|anti-imperialist]] and [[W:Anti-globalism|anti-globalist]] views on foreign policy. The platform is considered "left-conservative" or "left-authoritarian", as it combines economically [[W:Socialism|socialist]] values with elements of [[W:Cultural conservatism|cultural conservatism]] in regards to [[Immigration to Balisca|immigration]].

The platform originated as a split from the [[Revolutionary Front]], led by [[Josuè Subirà]] after the decision of the Front to support [[Zavier Bilal]] for reelection in the [[2024 Baliscan premiership election|2024 premiership race]], and he was joined several other long time members of the Revolutionary Front in establishing the platform. Subirà was ultimately defeated by Bilal by a seventeen point margin.

